+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Three reports show the code disagreeing with the README business rules: lower-case SKUs are refused as unknown, an order whose goods come to exactly €50.00 is charged shipping, and line VAT is rounded down instead of half up.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Catalogue lookups canonicalise the SKU (trim, upper case), so `lb-220` finds `LB-220`.
+- Shipping is free when goods (after every discount, before VAT) are €50.00 or more; today exactly €50.00 pays.
+- Line VAT is rounded half up to the cent (€1.99 at 22% gives €0.44, not €0.43).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `order-pricing`: product lookup by SKU, free-shipping threshold and per-line VAT rounding, as the README documents them.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/catalog.ts` (`find`), `src/shipping.ts` (`shippingCost`), `src/tax.ts` (`lineVat`); tests under `test/`. No API changes.
